.pyre/

# Local working artifacts — not product code, never commit (public repo).
# Scoped to the specific directories rather than all of `docs/`, so a future
# real documentation directory is not silently swallowed.
docs/superpowers/
docs/csv-samples/

# Report output from running the CLI locally. These contain real usernames,
# emails and usage figures from whatever deployment they were generated
# against, so they must never reach this public repo.
# Matched by filename rather than by directory, so they are caught wherever
# --csv-dir happens to point. The committed samples live in docs/csv-samples/,
# which is already ignored above.
/growth_report.html
comet-chargeback-report*.json
growth_users.csv
growth_workspaces.csv
growth_org_kpis.csv
